23:16:27 said  The viewport toolbar buttons now have rounded corners and a small coloured icon each. Almost every menu item now does something:
23:16:27 said  - **Render:** all the render modes.
23:16:27 said  - **Show:** Bones, Normals and hiding back faces.
23:16:27 said  - **Forces and collision objects:** you can add Direction and Magnet forces that bend the branches as they grow, plus Sphere and Capsule collision objects. Pick one by pressing it in the viewport, then move, turn or resize it by dragging, depending on the Gizmo setting.
23:16:27 said  - **Other tools:** Wind sways the tree, Season shifts the leaf colours, AO turns on shading, Collision removes overlapping leaves, and Export saves the tree as an OBJ file.
23:16:27 said  Three things aren't built yet:
23:16:27 said  - Nodes (editing single branches).
23:16:27 said  - The Mesh force.
23:16:27 said  - Fronds, Zones, Targets and Proxies: these toggles have nothing to show, because TreeCraft doesn't grow those yet.
23:16:28 said  The app builds and passes every check. I looked at several render modes, the bones and a force bending the tree in screenshots. The Wind sway, the Export file and dragging objects in the viewport haven't been tried yet. How each of these tools works is my own design; I didn't read SpeedTree's code for them this time.
