23:19:13 said  The viewport render modes now follow the original's own formulas, taken from the shader files SpeedTree installs in its render_modes folder (the program itself wasn't decompiled this time):
23:19:13 said  - Albedo Check and Subsurface Check now use SpeedTree's brightness limits and blue-to-red scale.
23:19:13 said  - Vertex Colors Red/Green/Blue show each channel in its own colour instead of grey.
23:19:13 said  - Phong, Blinn-Phong, Oren-Nayar and Lambert use the original's shine and roughness formulas.
23:19:13 said  - Flat is now Blinn-Phong lighting, but on the smooth surfaces, not SpeedTree's faceted ones.
23:19:13 said  - Overdraw adds faint red with each layer, Depth shows screen depth, and Texcoord Seams uses the original's pattern.
23:19:14 said  Lightmap and Shadow still can't match SpeedTree, because TreeCraft has no lightmap layout or shadows. The app builds and passes every check, the formulas are written up in the project notes, and the credits list those shader files as read but not copied.
