15:59:53 said  All three parts are in, and the app builds and passes every check:
15:59:53 said  - **New generators start plain.** Anything added from +Add now has no bending, no taper, the same length for every copy and no material, so it shows as plain grey until you choose a material yourself.
15:59:53 said  - **Full menu bar.** It now matches SpeedTree's: File, Edit, Tools, Window, Assets and Help, with their submenus and shortcuts. That includes recent files, step-numbered saves, saving with the picture files copied alongside, exporting the selected part or a picture of the view, undoing a selection, scene scaling and window layouts. A few items, such as FBX cameras, the growth wizard and SpeedTree's web links, have nothing behind them in TreeCraft yet, so they show a message saying so.
15:59:53 said  - **Save warning.** Closing the window, Exit, New, Open or Close with unsaved changes now asks "This tree has been modified, do you wish to save your changes?", and Yes opens the save window.
15:59:54 said  The automatic checks don't open the new menus or the warning, so those haven't been clicked through yet. Which menu each item sits under is my best guess from the original program, and how branches bend and taper is still estimated.
