22:41:29 said  The program file is now called TreeCraft and has its own icon: a branching cream tree with green and gold leaves on a blue-teal tile. The old pinned shortcut keeps its plain name and icon, so unpin it and pin TreeCraft again. TreeCraft now opens maximized, and if you close it at a smaller size it reopens at that size, though I haven't tried that by closing and reopening it.
22:41:29 said  In the Generation graph, each generator is now a box with a coloured header for its kind and a count like "364 leaves", joined to the others by blue curved wires. To link two nodes, drag from a box's top or bottom dot onto another box. Right-clicking empty space opens the full Add menu, so every node type can be created from the graph. Forces and collision objects now appear as boxes of their own beside the tree. You can change the graph's background, box, header and wire colours under Preferences, Themes, on a new "Node Editor" tab.
