06:24:24 said  All five changes from the screenshot are in, and the app builds and passes every check:
06:24:24 said  - **Render menu:** it now has "WireShaded", which draws the edges over the normal shaded view, and "Wireframe", which shows only see-through lines.
06:24:24 said  - **No default materials:** the default Bark and Leaf materials are gone, so a new session starts with an empty material list.
06:24:24 said  - **Texture slots:** all ten slots now shrink to fit the panel without scrolling. I checked this in a picture of the app.
06:24:24 said  - **Curves:** every number setting has green (parent), blue (distribution) and yellow (profile) curve buttons; clicking one opens a small curve editor. These curves change how the tree grows, and they are saved with the tree.
06:24:24 said  - Parent: varies the value along the parent branch.
06:24:24 said  - Distribution: varies it from the first child to the last.
06:24:24 said  - Profile: varies it along each branch's own length. It only affects gravity, the two noise settings and radius, and on Frequency or Number it controls where the children appear along the parent. On every other setting the profile curve has no effect.
06:24:24 said  - **Node and Freehand:** both modes now work.
06:24:24 said  - Node mode (Tab switches to it and back): click one branch or leaf in the 3D view to change just that one — its length, thickness, angle and roll, or hide it.
06:24:24 said  - Freehand: drag in the 3D view to draw a branch. Start the drag on an existing branch to grow from it. If no branch generator is selected, it makes a new "Hand Drawn" one.
06:24:25 said  I haven't tried the curve editor, Node clicking or Freehand drawing myself, and the automatic checks don't touch them either. Give those three a quick try first. Branch bending and taper are still estimated rather than taken from SpeedTree.
