14:34:01 said  All five changes from the screenshot are in, and the app builds and passes every check:
14:34:01 said  - **Materials, assigned by hand:** a generator's Material tab now has SpeedTree's Materials lists — Branch and Extension — with − / + buttons. Each entry has a Material choice ("Inherited" means the parent branch's) and a Weight; each branch picks one entry by weight. An empty list draws plain grey. The Extension list is kept but does nothing yet, since TreeCraft has no branch extensions.
14:34:01 said  - **No green tint:** the green came from a "spring" season colour that was switched on by default. Season now starts at "None", and the lighting is uncoloured, so materials show their texture's own colours.
14:34:01 said  - **Clicking meshes:** clicking a branch or leaf in the 3D view (without dragging) selects its generator. Double-clicking also centres and zooms the camera on that spot, and the view then rotates around it.
14:34:01 said  - **UV preview:** the UV tab now has a preview under the UV settings. It has a "Show texture" switch and a Diffuse / Normal / Opacity choice, and it redraws as you change the UV values.
14:34:01 said  - **Gloss → Roughness:** Gloss is renamed Roughness everywhere (white = rough, black = glossy), and a Roughness picture now affects the 3D view.
14:34:01 said  I checked the Materials list and UV preview in pictures of the app, but I haven't tried clicking or double-clicking meshes, and the automatic checks don't touch that either.
