15:47:47 said  The viewport now has a "Shading: Studio" button at the top right, with Studio as the default. Clicking it opens a drop-down with Studio, MatCap and Flat and a ball preview, which stays hidden until you click. MatCap offers five looks to pick from (Clay, Chrome, Jade, Red wax, Ceramic), and Flat shows the textures with no lighting. MatCap and Flat only apply in the Render menu's Standard mode.
15:47:47 said  There's also a view gizmo at the top right: click an axis to look along it, click it again to look from the other side, or drag its background to turn the view. It replaces the small axis marker that sat in the bottom-right corner. In Preferences > Viewport you can pick one of four designs (Axis balls, Arrows, View cube, Minimal dots) or hide it, and set its size.
15:47:47 said  In the Front, Back, Left, Right, Top and Bottom views, dragging now pans instead of rotating, and the wheel still zooms. A new "Rotate fixed views" option in Preferences turns rotating back on.
15:47:47 said  The app builds and passes all checks, and I looked at pictures of the shading menu, MatCap, and the Axis-ball and View-cube gizmos. The automatic checks don't click the gizmo or drag in the fixed views, so try those yourself.
