00:22:19 said  All three changes are in, and the app builds and passes every check:
00:22:19 said  - **No end caps:** branches and trunks are now open at both ends by default. A "Cap ends" tick box in the Skin section closes them if you want.
00:22:19 said  - **Curve buttons:** each setting now shows only the curve buttons SpeedTree gives it, read from SpeedTree's own program. For example, Length has only a Parent curve, while Gravity has Parent and Distribution. That covers about 200 settings; for the rest I couldn't read SpeedTree's choice, so they show a Parent curve where the old table marked them as curve settings, and no curve button otherwise.
00:22:19 said  - **Curve editor:** it now has SpeedTree's layout. You can move it by its title bar and resize it from any edge or corner. A "P" pin keeps it open; unpinned, clicking elsewhere closes it.
00:22:19 said  - It has SpeedTree's controls: a Parent level choice, a Draw button for drawing the curve freehand, SpeedTree's 23 presets, and X/Y boxes for the selected point.
00:22:19 said  - Right-clicking the graph gives SpeedTree's menu: insert normal, step or sharp-corner points, delete, scale, flip, select all, copy and paste. I added a "Remove curve" option to that menu, since SpeedTree's menu has no way to drop a curve.
00:22:19 said  - The preset names are SpeedTree's, but their shapes and the scale amount are my guesses.
00:22:20 said  I saw the editor and the per-setting curve buttons in a test picture, but the automatic checks don't use the editor, so dragging, drawing and the menu are untested.
