10:44:32 said  All three changes are in, and the app builds and passes every check:
10:44:32 said  - **Curve presets:** the curve editor was closing when you picked a preset whose list item sat below the window, so the choice was lost. That's fixed, and a test now confirms all 23 presets give a valid curve.
10:44:32 said  - **Number boxes:** clicking or double-clicking a number box now selects the whole value, so typing replaces it.
10:44:32 said  - **+/- buttons:** number settings that vary in SpeedTree now have a +/- button at the end of the row, which turns pink and shows the amount once it's set. It opens a Variance Settings window like SpeedTree's, with Variance, Distribution (Uniform or Gaussian), and a Cohesive-to-Random slider with Scale and Offset. The old separate "+/-" rows are gone, and the tree now uses these settings for every setting that has one. How Cohesion, Scale and Offset spread the values is my own guess, since I couldn't read SpeedTree's formula.
