11:14:14 said  Most of the list is done, but "make every parameter work" is only partly done (details below). The app builds and passes all checks.
11:14:14 said  - **Number arrows:** every number field now has left and right arrows. Whole numbers step by 1, and other values step by a round amount such as 0.01 or 0.05, depending on the setting's range.
11:14:14 said  - **Type menus:** Skin Type and the other Style settings are now drop-downs with SpeedTree's own choices. I read these from SpeedTree's program. The choice names are certain; the order of the leaf-arrangement (Phyllotaxy) list is my best guess.
11:14:14 said  - **Parameters that work now:** about 16 more settings now actually shape the tree:
11:14:14 said  - Length "+ % of radius", Roll, Ancestor, Straightness and Twist.
11:14:14 said  - All the Prune settings and the Break settings.
11:14:14 said  - Late noise Smooth and the noise Seed.
11:14:14 said  - Skin Type "Spine only".
11:14:14 said  - **Still dummies:** most other settings remain faint and do nothing yet, including most of Skin, Season, Wind, Growth, Displacement, LOD and the leaf settings.
11:14:14 said  - **Curve presets:** these really were broken. The editor was swallowing your click on any list item that sat over its own window. Presets, the Parent level list and the right-click menu now work, and the Variance window's list had the same fix.
11:14:14 said  - **Curve points:** they are easier to grab and drag.
11:14:14 said  - **How curves behave:**
11:14:14 said  - Each setting's second curve now works along the branch's own length, as SpeedTree's radius and gravity curves do. Before, it compared one branch with its neighbours.
11:14:14 said  - Parent curves on trunks now vary across the trunks.
11:14:14 said  - **Start-menu icon:** the program file already carried the icon; your old pin just keeps the blank picture Windows remembered for it. TreeCraft now adds its own "TreeCraft" shortcut with the icon to the Start menu the first time it starts. Unpin the old "treecraft" entry and pin the new one.
11:14:14 said  - **Splash screen:** TreeCraft now opens on a splash screen for about two and a half seconds: a tree grows from trunk to leaves under a dusk sky, beside the "TreeCraft" title and a loading bar. You can click to skip it after half a second. I checked how it looks in a picture.
11:14:15 said  I haven't tried the presets, the dragging or the new arrows by hand, and the automatic checks don't touch them.
