01:25:19 said  All five changes from your picture are in, and the app builds and passes its checks; most of the new Skin and Spine settings, though, are my own approximations rather than SpeedTree's exact rules.
01:25:19 said  - **Number fields:** the dial is on the left, and the left and right arrows now sit on either side of the number, in every number field in the app.
01:25:19 said  - **No limits:** Sweep, First and Last accept any value. First below 0 or Last above 1 means fewer branches near that end, because spots off the branch are skipped.
01:25:19 said  - **Copy and Paste:** every group header in the Properties panel (Spine, Skin, UV Mapping, Lightmap and so on) has two small buttons, two sheets for Copy and a clipboard for Paste. Copy takes the numbers, checkboxes and drop-downs shown in that group. Paste stays greyed out until you've copied that same group, and the curves and +/- variance settings don't come along.
01:25:19 said  - **Wireframe:** the WireShaded and Wireframe lines are thicker and darker by default. Preferences > Viewport now has Wire thickness, a colour for each mode, and how much brighter the selected trunk, branch or leaf's lines are.
01:25:19 said  - **Spine and Skin tabs:** every setting on both tabs now does something; none are shown faint any more.
01:25:19 said  - Two come straight from SpeedTree's program. Length kill ratio removes branches that are too long for their thickness. For Length compensation I found SpeedTree's formula but not what it applies it to, so I used it to thin short, stubby branches.
01:25:19 said  - The rest (Welding, Squash, Splits, Subdivision, Alignment, Unify and others) do what their names suggest, but I couldn't find SpeedTree's exact formulas, so they won't match it number for number.
01:25:19 said  - Shape scale and Stop shape control only work once you set the parent's Shape Control Size > Absolute above 0. That keeps your existing trees from changing.
01:25:19 said  The automatic checks don't click through any of this, and I haven't tested Copy/Paste, the arrows or the new settings by hand. I only looked at pictures of the Spine and Skin tabs and the thicker wires, which looked right. The mechanics check passed but notes it hasn't measured TreeCraft against SpeedTree's actual results.
01:25:20 said  The safety rules wouldn't let me delete a scratch folder of test pictures; you can delete `app/tmp_crops` yourself.
