01:53:52 said  All three changes are in, and the app builds and passes its checks; the UV preview fix is based on my best guess at the cause, which I couldn't reproduce.
01:53:52 said  - **Spine only:** a generator set to Spine only now shows in the viewport as a yellow line with a mark at each segment, so the marks match the count set under Segments. It gets brighter when selected. Its node in the graph has a black header, reads "spine only", and carries a round black badge with a yellow chain of links. I checked both in a picture.
01:53:52 said  - **Segments tab:** every setting now works and none are faint. The two Length settings set how many segments a branch has, and the old separate "Length segments" row is gone because "+ Relative" now does that job. SpeedTree's program doesn't show its formulas for these, so they're my approximations:
01:53:52 said  - Accuracy controls how finely the branch shape is grown.
01:53:52 said  - Weld scalar puts more segments near the base.
01:53:52 said  - Optimization drops segments where the branch runs nearly straight.
01:53:52 said  - Radial "+ Relative" adds segments around thicker branches.
01:53:52 said  - **UV preview:** the likely cause was a branch whose Materials list starts with "Inherited". Its bark takes the parent's material, but the preview found no material of its own and showed nothing. The preview now follows "Inherited" up to the parent, the same way the bark does.
01:53:53 said  One side effect: trees grow in a different number of steps now, so existing trees may look slightly different. I haven't tried the copy/paste case, the new Segments settings or the arrows by hand. The scratch picture folder `app/tmp_crops` can still be deleted.
