06:01:24 said  All three changes are in, and the app builds and passes its checks.
06:01:24 said  - **Radial curves:** the blue Radial curve now changes how many segments go round the branch along its length. In a picture with a falling curve, the trunk was dense at the bottom and sparse at the top.
06:01:24 said  - The green Parent curve was already wired in, but on a single trunk it reads only the start of the curve, so redrawing it shows no change.
06:01:24 said  - **Default curves:** SpeedTree's program stores a starting shape for every setting's curves, and I read them all out. A new curve now starts in that shape, and settings whose starting shape isn't flat use it even before you open the curve.
06:01:24 said  - Noise Late Amount's along-the-branch curve now starts as Linear growth, so the lower trunk stays smooth. SpeedTree doesn't store one for this setting, so this follows your request.
06:01:24 said  - The trunk now looks smoother at the base by default.
06:01:24 said  - I left Radius out: SpeedTree's default there is Linear decay, but TreeCraft's Tip radius (taper) already narrows the branch, so it would thin twice.
06:01:24 said  - **Node Editor page in Preferences:**
06:01:24 said  - Five node styles, each shown as a small sample you click: Rectangle (the current one), Rounded, Circle, Ellipse and Hexagon.
06:01:24 said  - Background colour.
06:01:24 said  - Grid as dots, lines, crosses or none, with a spacing control.
06:01:24 said  - Wire style (curved, straight or angled) and wire thickness.
06:01:24 said  - Node size, and whether nodes show their counts.
06:01:24 said  I checked the varying radial count and the Preferences page in pictures. After the first picture I moved the Circle style's names beside the circle to keep them clear of the wires, and I haven't looked at that change since. I haven't tried the other Node Editor settings or the default curves by hand.
