02:26:34 said  All six parts are in; the app builds and passes its checks. One gap: TreeCraft doesn't save your lighting settings yet, so it starts on Daylight each time.
02:26:34 said  - **Lighting from below:** this was a real bug. The branch surfaces were built inside-out, so the light reached the bark from underneath. The tops of branches are lit now, and the default sun sits 45° up, like mid-morning or mid-afternoon.
02:26:34 said  - **Lighting button:** it now opens Preferences on the Lighting page, which has SpeedTree's own settings.
02:26:34 said  - Environment: the light's colour and intensity, and the Sky, Horizon and Ground colours with their intensity.
02:26:34 said  - Ambient Occlusion: Brightness, Contrast, Min, Max, and Render/Clear buttons.
02:26:34 said  - Shadows: Quality and Ground weight.
02:26:34 said  - Preset: SpeedTree's five presets (Daylight, Bright sun, Dusk, Overcast, Moonlight), with the values copied from SpeedTree's own preset file.
02:26:34 said  - **Sky background:** the viewport now has a SpeedTree-style sky above the horizon and ground colour below it, and this is the default. You can switch back to the old dark look under Preferences > Themes > Background.
02:26:34 said  - **Ground and shadows:** a ground disc sits under the grid and catches the tree's shadow, including the leaf shapes. Turn it on or off in Preferences > Viewport or the Show menu.
02:26:34 said  - Higher shadow quality softens the shadow's edge. It isn't a full shadow system: shadows don't fall on the tree itself.
02:26:34 said  - **Light controller:** a bulb under the navigation gizmo shows the light's intensity. Click it, then drag in the viewport to move the sun, and click again to stop. The mouse wheel over it changes intensity, and right-click opens the Lighting page.
02:26:34 said  - The fan below it does nothing yet, as you asked.
02:26:34 said  - **Height indicator:** an orange-and-white measuring staff stands beside the tree, with heights marked along it and the total height on a tag at the top. It only appears once the tree has a generator, and Show > Height indicator hides it. The numbers have no unit, because TreeCraft doesn't define one.
02:26:34 said  I checked the corrected lighting, the sky, the shadows, the staff and the Lighting page in pictures. I haven't clicked through the presets, the light controller or the new toggles.
02:26:35 said  My earlier test pictures had changed your node style setting to Circle without my noticing. I've set it back to Rectangle.
