03:01:31 said  All four changes from your picture are in, and the app builds and passes its checks.
03:01:31 said  - **Node Editor settings:** they now sit in Preferences > Themes > Node Editor, under the node colours. The separate Node Editor page is gone.
03:01:31 said  - **Person for scale:** redrawn as an ordinary adult standing at ease, with weight on one leg and arms relaxed. It's still 1.8 units tall and is my own figure, not SpeedTree's.
03:01:31 said  - **Shadow:** it's now hard and drawn once as a solid shade of the ground's colour, so overlapping parts can no longer stack up and flicker. It sits just under the grid, so the grid lines show over it.
03:01:31 said  - It does have a limit: being solid, it uses the ground colour or the plain colour below the horizon. That can look slightly off where it falls past the edge of the ground disc.
03:01:31 said  - **Shadow side and presets:** Light > Shadows has a new "Shadow side light" setting that lets some sunlight wrap round onto the shaded side. It's on a little by default, so the dark side is lighter than before. Below it, a "Shadow presets" list offers five looks:
03:01:31 said  - Uncharted style (soft)
03:01:31 said  - Red Dead style (realistic)
03:01:31 said  - Zelda style (bright, painterly)
03:01:31 said  - The Last of Us style (moody)
03:01:31 said  - Ghost of Tsushima style (warm, airy)
03:01:31 said  These are my own interpretations of those games' looks, not values taken from them.
