12:16:33 said  All three changes are in, and the app builds and passes its checks. Two of the new settings don't do what their names suggest (details below).
12:16:33 said  - **Height figure:** the person for scale is now the reference figure from your picture, cut out from its white background.
12:16:33 said  - **Shadow styles:** "Default" is now at the top of the list, and "(custom)" moves to the bottom.
12:16:33 said  - **Preferences:** five new pages, General, Tree Window, Property Bar, Render and Data, with the setting names copied from SpeedTree's program. I chose the starting values myself, because I didn't find SpeedTree's own.
12:16:33 said  - **General:** Display scaling enlarges or shrinks the whole interface. The node-edit warning appears when a change moves a generator's nodes. Autosave keeps a copy of an unsaved tree every few minutes, which Welcome > Recover Last Session brings back.
12:16:33 said  - **Tree Window:** the selection highlight can hide while you change a value. You can turn the fan on or off and set the height marker size. The Maya and 3ds Max mouse controls work, and so do the reverse zoom, rotate and pan options.
12:16:33 said  - **Property Bar:** number fields can drop the dial. Opening one group can close the others, the panel can glide when scrolling, and an opened group scrolls to the top or just into view.
12:16:33 said  - **Render:** "Multi-sampling" smooths edges once TreeCraft is restarted. Max texture resolution reloads pictures at the new size. "Flip normals on backsides" changes how the backs of leaves are lit.
12:16:33 said  - **Data:** this page only says that TreeCraft never sends any data, so there's nothing to switch.
12:16:33 said  - **Shadow:** it's now drawn once as a picture and laid on the ground. That gives it smooth edges and should stop the flicker. "Shadow anti-aliasing samples" controls how smooth those edges are.
12:16:33 said  - **Two settings work differently from their names:**
12:16:33 said  - "Use multiple processors" only reads a tree's pictures in parallel when you open it.
12:16:33 said  - "Always use native file dialogs": TreeCraft's file windows are always the Windows ones. Turning this off just makes them open in the folder you used last.
12:16:33 said  I checked the new shadow, the figure, the Default style and the Tree Window page in pictures. I haven't tried the new settings by hand. Your preferences file has the node style set to Circle; I left it as it is in case you chose it, so tell me if you didn't.
