12:24:42 said  Both changes from your picture are in, and the app builds and passes its checks.
12:24:42 said  - **World origin:** a terracotta disc now sits at the world origin. When you select the Tree node it gets brighter and gains a yellow ring. Its colour can be changed under Preferences > Themes ("World origin").
12:24:42 said  - **Freehand controller:** Freehand mode now puts a bend controller on the selected trunk or branch generator.
12:24:42 said  - **Green top handle:** drag it to bend the generator from the pivot. The bend spreads along the blue band, so a longer band gives a gentler curve, and the angle shows beside the handle.
12:24:42 said  - **Blue band:** drag it to slide the whole controller up or down the generator.
12:24:42 said  - **Pink pivot handle:** drag it to stretch or shorten the band; the bend always starts there.
12:24:42 said  - **Properties panel:** sliders for the pivot, the top, the bend angle, its direction and its shape, plus "Reset bend" and "Reset generator to default".
12:24:42 said  - **Behaviour you might not expect:**
12:24:42 said  - The controller sits on one of the generator's branches, but every branch from that generator bends the same way in the world. On a side-branch generator, that may not be what you want.
12:24:42 said  - Drawing branches by hand now needs Ctrl held while dragging.
12:24:43 said  I checked the controller on a bent trunk and the origin disc in pictures. I haven't dragged the handles by hand, and I didn't try the "Reset generator to default" button.
